{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792923602,"nonce":"X4UuCESNGAoW7AQF7HxlCgIwIf8=","title":"LSP: Wren in caribou-lsp","message":"Part of 1626b90d930d209e848220743e00494408af449d2cdabdddea70f6c0a5337545 (caribou lsp).\n\nwlift-lsp (wren_lift/crates/wlift_lsp) is a binary on tower-lsp. It gives\ndiagnostics from the parser and resolve_with_prelude, hover, definition,\ncompletion on `.` and code lenses. Its sema binds imported names without\nchecking that the module exists.\n\n- **A library target.** wlift_lsp gains a lib target whose analysis\n  caribou-lsp calls from its own loop, instead of copying the handlers. This\n  is a change in WrenLift, coordinated with that repository.\n- **Namespaced imports against the registry.** Caribou checks\n  `import \"game:tally\" for score` against the project's registry:\n  - a missing module, or a name the module does not export, is reported;\n  - a found one gets hover, definition and completion from its interface,\n    for a Python, Lua, Haxe or plugin module alike.\n- **What WrenLift resolves stays WrenLift's.** `@hatch:` packages and\n  relative imports resolve as WrenLift does today.","files":null}]}